5. Aggrieved by the said judgment and award, the injured claimant has preferred this appeal, in which it is contended that, he sustained fracture of bicondylar tibia; he was admitted in the hospital for five days from 03.08.2020 to 08.08.2020; he underwent operation and bone grafting was done;
the doctor assessed the disability at 40% to the limb and 22% to the whole body, but the Tribunal has taken it only 10%; he was earning Rs.25,000/- per month by doing milk vending and by way of tuition classes, but the Tribunal has taken his income NC: 2025:KHC-K:6684 HC-KAR only at Sangamesh vs Ganapati And Anr on 4 November, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/179500622/
2 Rs.11,000/- per month.

